                <pb facs="0206" n="98" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg98"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr.
                            Thompson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-01-09"><hi rendition="#italic">January 9,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Gresham directs Mr. Thompson to induce, by cooperation with the commanding
                    officer of the forces of the United States, and if possible with others, the
                    insurgents to designate a place, if such a place can be found, at which vessels
                    of neutral nations may, without interfering with mililitary operations, take and
                    discharge cargoes in safety.</p>
            </div>
